{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KVSqybmr3mxP2JFey4FJWf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# QuantAgent-sft — Implementation: paper runtime hardening\n2\t\n3\t## Overview\n4\t- Scoped scheduler-managed `ActivePosition` rows to the paper environment instead of relying on the model default.\n5\t- Persisted `trade_id` when the paper scheduler opens an active position so the `signal -> order -> trade -> position` chain remains reconstructible.\n6\t- Hardened scheduler heartbeat state transitions so recovered stale `running` rows and fatal cycle failures become observable.\n7\t- Updated the Streamlit paper runtime view to distinguish `running`, `stuck`, and `error` states instead of inferring health only from recency.\n8\t\n9\t## Approach\n10\t- `quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py`\n11\t  - Added optional environment context to `PositionMonitor`.\n12\t  - Filtered active-position lookups by environment when that context is present.\n13\t  - Persisted the resolved environment when opening a position.\n14\t- `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py`\n15\t  - Instantiated `PositionMonitor` with `Environment.PAPER`.\n16\t  - Resolved `trade_id` from the filled order before creating the `ActivePosition`.\n17\t  - Reset heartbeat completion fields on new cycle start, flag stale recovered `running` rows, and added explicit heartbeat `error` updates for fatal cycle failures.\n18\t  - Scoped `last_trade_id` lookup to the scheduler environment.\n19\t- `apps/streamlit/views/paper_trading.py`\n20\t  - Surfaced heartbeat `error_message`.\n21\t  - Mapped recent `running` heartbeats to `Running`, stale `running` heartbeats to `Stuck`, and explicit heartbeat failures to `Error`.\n22\t\n23\t## Deviations\n24\t- No test files were modified in this run because the executor contract for this phase explicitly disabled `write_tests`.\n25\t\n26\t## Validation\n27\t- `/mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/test_vje_paper_trading_view.py -q`\n28\t- `/mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python -m ruff check --fix apps/streamlit/views/paper_trading.py quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py quantagent/trading/scheduler.py docs/06_implementation/QuantAgent-sft-IM-paper-runtime-hardening.md`\n29\t- `/mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python -m compileall -q quantagent apps`\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2e7c456-35f5-44fa-bc39-3f5f6a9f15ef","uuid":"9f3e432c-14b7-48fa-9bba-3ebda1df07ff","timestamp":"2026-05-14T07:39:08.130Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/06_implementation/QuantAgent-sft-IM-paper-runtime-hardening.md","content":"# QuantAgent-sft — Implementation: paper runtime hardening\n\n## Overview\n- Scoped scheduler-managed `ActivePosition` rows to the paper environment instead of relying on the model default.\n- Persisted `trade_id` when the paper scheduler opens an active position so the `signal -> order -> trade -> position` chain remains reconstructible.\n- Hardened scheduler heartbeat state transitions so recovered stale `running` rows and fatal cycle failures become observable.\n- Updated the Streamlit paper runtime view to distinguish `running`, `stuck`, and `error` states instead of inferring health only from recency.\n\n## Approach\n- `quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py`\n  - Added optional environment context to `PositionMonitor`.\n  - Filtered active-position lookups by environment when that context is present.\n  - Persisted the resolved environment when opening a position.\n- `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py`\n  - Instantiated `PositionMonitor` with `Environment.PAPER`.\n  - Resolved `trade_id` from the filled order before creating the `ActivePosition`.\n  - Reset heartbeat completion fields on new cycle start, flag stale recovered `running` rows, and added explicit heartbeat `error` updates for fatal cycle failures.\n  - Scoped `last_trade_id` lookup to the scheduler environment.\n- `apps/streamlit/views/paper_trading.py`\n  - Surfaced heartbeat `error_message`.\n  - Mapped recent `running` heartbeats to `Running`, stale `running` heartbeats to `Stuck`, and explicit heartbeat failures to `Error`.\n\n## Deviations\n- No test files were modified in this run because the executor contract for this phase explicitly disabled `write_tests`.\n\n## Validation\n- `/mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/test_vje_paper_trading_view.py -q`\n- `/mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python -m ruff check --fix apps/streamlit/views/paper_trading.py quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py quantagent/trading/scheduler.py docs/06_implementation/QuantAgent-sft-IM-paper-runtime-hardening.md`\n- `/mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python -m compileall -q quantagent apps`\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}}}
