{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01HX31FPz3qFRtstG6rzjJ75","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now I have a thorough understanding of the system. Let me create the planning artifacts:\n\n1. `docs/01_requirements/QuantAgent-aki-RQ-paper-pilot.md` - Requirements document\n2. `docs/02_planning/QuantAgent-aki-PL-paper-pilot.md` - Planning document\n3. `docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-aki-AC-paper-pilot.md` - Acceptance criteria\n4. `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-aki/20260514T073839Z-QuantAgent-aki-planner/result.json`\n\n\n5. `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-aki/20260514T073839Z-QuantAgent-aki-planner/run-report.md`\n\nThen I'll add a Beads comment. For the pilot, I'm going with RSI and FiftyTwoWeek strategies since the requirements call for 1-3 strategies, keeping the universe small with just SPY and AAPL to minimize complexity and cost.\n\nThe execution approach is to run 3 scheduler cycles directly without APScheduler overhead, then collect evidence from the actual paper trading execution—heartbeats, trades, signals, orders, and positions captured from the database after the cycles complete. The implementer will need a pilot runner script that initializes the scheduler with controlled settings, drives the cycles, and formats the results into a readiness report. I should keep the implementation details flexible rather than over-specifying the exact approach.\n\nNow I'm thinking through what needs to be in the planning document itself: preconditions that must be met before the pilot runs, the scope of strategies and universe, the evidence capture format, and a readiness report template. The critical question is whether the pilot can actually execute in the local environment—checking that the database is accessible, at least one M1 strategy can generate signals on the pilot universe, and PaperBroker can fill orders. Given the partial QA validator results, there are known issues to account for.